WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.597 --> 00:00:13.681
them away!"

2
00:00:14.161 --> 00:00:15.142
Zira shouted again.

3
00:00:15.162 --> 00:00:17.364
"I can't believe this is happening!"

4
00:00:17.864 --> 00:00:19.305
Zann thought, outraged.

5
00:00:19.325 --> 00:00:21.827
"Release us right now!"

6
00:00:22.328 --> 00:00:24.670
Perda cried, struggling against her shackles.

7
00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:28.153
Zann saw one of the large men heading toward him.

8
00:00:28.173 --> 00:00:29.534
"Don't touch me!"

9
00:00:29.894 --> 00:00:30.514
Zann yelled.

10
00:00:31.255 --> 00:00:32.136
Zira smirked.

11
00:00:32.668 --> 00:00:35.189
"You look like a sturdy kid, Zann."

12
00:00:35.769 --> 00:00:36.950
She glanced at the goon.

13
00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:42.112
"Take him to the mines in the mountains beyond the lowland swamps.

14
00:00:42.772 --> 00:00:44.653
He can make himself useful there.

15
00:00:45.413 --> 00:00:46.794
Krub, go with them."

16
00:00:46.814 --> 00:00:49.255
"No, stop!"

17
00:00:49.715 --> 00:00:50.255
Zann said.

18
00:00:50.815 --> 00:00:54.517
The goon grabbed one of Zann's arms, and Krub grabbed the other.

19
00:00:55.097 --> 00:00:57.858
Zann struggled, even though he knew it was no use.

20
00:00:58.739 --> 00:01:02.936
As they dragged him away, he glanced back at Perda and Mellis.

21
00:01:02.956 --> 00:01:04.117
Perda's eyes met his.

22
00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:06.959
Zann wished he could break away and save her.

23
00:01:07.579 --> 00:01:10.241
Suddenly he felt words forming in his mind.

24
00:01:10.261 --> 00:01:12.643
"Perda is sending me a mental message!"

25
00:01:13.043 --> 00:01:13.443
he thought.

26
00:01:13.463 --> 00:01:16.745
"She must have been inspired by the message she got from Zira."

27
00:01:17.986 --> 00:01:24.691
Her words were faint and muddled, but Zann was pretty sure he understood them: Look for other wormholes.

28
00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:27.713
I'll find you and Mellis when I can get away.

29
00:01:28.813 --> 00:01:30.815
Zann nodded and Perda smiled.

30
00:01:31.515 --> 00:01:34.488
Zann smiled back, glad that they were a team.

31
00:01:35.389 --> 00:01:38.289
"What are you grinning about, you weird kid?"

32
00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:41.050
Krub growled, yanking on Zann's arm.

33
00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:44.871
"In case you didn't notice, you're a prisoner.

34
00:01:45.471 --> 00:01:48.752
And you're about to learn what hard work is like!"

35
00:01:49.453 --> 00:01:52.133
He laughed nastily, and the goon joined in.

36
00:01:53.474 --> 00:01:54.434
Zann ignored them.

37
00:01:54.874 --> 00:01:58.535
Now he was looking for Zing, but he couldn't see him anywhere.

38
00:01:58.555 --> 00:02:03.080
"We have a long walk ahead of us," the goon said.

39
00:02:03.620 --> 00:02:05.181
"Might as well get started."

40
00:02:05.961 --> 00:02:06.901
Krub smirked.

41
00:02:06.921 --> 00:02:10.042
"No walking for us today, my friend.

42
00:02:10.803 --> 00:02:13.783
Zira taught me how to travel by magic."

43
00:02:13.803 --> 00:02:15.264
"She did?"

44
00:02:15.744 --> 00:02:18.265
The goon looked impressed and a little nervous.

45
00:02:18.285 --> 00:02:19.845
"Is it safe?"

46
00:02:19.865 --> 00:02:26.027
"Safer than hiking through lands occupied by gorzogs and rock trompers," Krub replied.

47
00:02:26.047 --> 00:02:34.682
"Rub your hands together, like this He and the other man dropped their hold on Zann and created

48
00:02:34.762 --> 00:02:37.283
friction. Then they grabbed him again.

49
00:02:37.303 --> 00:02:39.885
"Zap!" Krub shouted.

50
00:02:40.845 --> 00:02:42.566
They landed in a patch of brambles.

51
00:02:42.586 --> 00:02:46.908
"Ouch," the goon said, yanking a thorn from his hand.

52
00:02:46.928 --> 00:02:48.930
"Where are we?"

53
00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:51.311
Zann wondered the same thing.

54
00:02:52.091 --> 00:02:55.493
All he saw were trees, rocky land, and scrubby plants.

55
00:02:56.854 --> 00:02:57.915
Krub looked around.

56
00:02:57.935 --> 00:03:00.236
"I recognize this place.

57
00:03:01.056 --> 00:03:03.217
We're only a third of the way to the mines.

58
00:03:03.998 --> 00:03:07.019
Zira said it might require several zaps to get to them."

59
00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:08.760
He frowned.

60
00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:10.842
"I guess she was right.

61
00:03:11.642 --> 00:03:12.903
It's late and I'm tired.

62
00:03:13.483 --> 00:03:16.405
We'll camp here tonight and zap the rest of the way tomorrow."

63
00:03:16.425 --> 00:03:19.406
"Camp?" Zann thought with a shiver.

64
00:03:20.007 --> 00:03:22.928
He didn't relish the idea of camping out with these two.

65
00:03:23.509 --> 00:03:24.869
But he didn't have a choice.

66
00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:29.472
Krub used magic to create simple tents for himself and the goon.

67
00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:33.322
But Zann was left to sleep outside on the hard ground.

68
00:03:34.442 --> 00:03:36.964
The men built a fire and ate the food they'd brought.

69
00:03:37.504 --> 00:03:42.387
They also pulled out flasks of foul-smelling liquid that they swilled with enthusiasm.

70
00:03:43.027 --> 00:03:46.329
Krub gave Zann a piece of jerky and a few sips of water.

71
00:03:47.169 --> 00:03:50.571
The jerky tasted like dirt, and the water was stale.

72
00:03:51.571 --> 00:03:56.814
After the sun went down, strange creatures made noises in the trees all around the camp.

73
00:03:57.475 --> 00:03:59.916
Zann flinched at every grunt and howl.

74
00:04:00.748 --> 00:04:06.171
But he did his best to ignore them, along with the men's talk and laughter as they continued

75
00:04:06.251 --> 00:04:07.431
drinking from their flasks.

76
00:04:08.392 --> 00:04:13.814
"I need to get some rest," Zann told himself, trying to get comfortable on the rough, rocky ground.

77
00:04:13.834 --> 00:04:16.276
"I want to be ready for anything tomorrow."

78
00:04:18.577 --> 00:04:21.458
He was drifting off to sleep when a howl woke him.

79
00:04:21.958 --> 00:04:25.140
A second later an animal stepped into the firelight.

80
00:04:26.056 --> 00:04:30.978
It was the same size as Zing, with brown fur and sly red eyes.

81
00:04:30.998 --> 00:04:32.319
"A chupo!"

82
00:04:32.719 --> 00:04:33.479
Krub exclaimed.

83
00:04:33.959 --> 00:04:35.600
The goon picked up a large stick.

84
00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:37.541
"I'll chase it away."

85
00:04:37.561 --> 00:04:40.582
"No—wait." Krub grinned.

86
00:04:40.602 --> 00:04:43.143
"It isn't interested in us.

87
00:04:43.803 --> 00:04:44.844
Just the boy.

88
00:04:45.884 --> 00:04:48.325
Maybe we should let it have him, eh?

89
00:04:49.306 --> 00:04:51.146
Even chupos have to eat."

90
00:04:52.067 --> 00:04:54.788
Zann sat up, struggling against the shackles.

91
00:04:55.492 --> 00:04:56.193
"Come on, guys.

92
00:04:56.713 --> 00:04:57.514
This isn't funny."

93
00:04:58.214 --> 00:05:01.417
Krub and the goon laughed as the chupo crept closer.

94
00:05:02.578 --> 00:05:07.001
"Look, here comes the rest of the pack," Krub said.

95
00:05:07.722 --> 00:05:10.464
Several more chupos appeared out of the darkness.

96
00:05:11.285 --> 00:05:14.047
One stopped and stared fearfully toward the fire.

97
00:05:14.647 --> 00:05:17.069
But the rest were focused on Zann.

98
00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:20.592
He gulped as one of the creatures licked its chops.

99
00:05:21.693 --> 00:05:25.236
Zann could tell the two men were enjoying watching his terror.

100
00:05:26.104 --> 00:05:28.125
For a second he felt helpless.

101
00:05:28.845 --> 00:05:32.747
Then he realized something: He wasn't actually helpless.

102
00:05:33.347 --> 00:05:35.648
The shackles stopped him from moving freely.

103
00:05:36.269 --> 00:05:38.349
But they couldn't stop him from doing magic.

104
00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:43.572
Even if they were too tight to allow him to rub his hands together, he could still snap

105
00:05:43.612 --> 00:05:44.132
his fingers.

106
00:05:44.832 --> 00:05:47.453
He did so several times to build up friction.

107
00:05:47.473 --> 00:05:49.154
"Get back!"

108
00:05:49.394 --> 00:05:52.736
he blurted out, creating a fireball that shot toward the chupos.

109
00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:57.663
They ran away, howling with fear, and disappeared into the darkness.

110
00:05:57.683 --> 00:05:59.504
"Look at that!"

111
00:06:00.124 --> 00:06:01.866
Krub crowed with a hearty laugh.

112
00:06:01.886 --> 00:06:04.988
"The boy has some fire in him after all.

113
00:06:05.648 --> 00:06:06.068
Get it?

114
00:06:06.549 --> 00:06:08.130
Fire?" He grinned.

115
00:06:08.970 --> 00:06:11.452
The goon came over and slapped Zann on the back.

116
00:06:12.233 --> 00:06:14.514
"Well done, boy," he said.

117
00:06:14.534 --> 00:06:17.056
"That kind of courage deserves a drink."

118
00:06:17.917 --> 00:06:19.137
He held out his flask.

119
00:06:19.498 --> 00:06:22.740
Whatever was inside smelled even worse up close.

120
00:06:23.732 --> 00:06:25.354
"No thanks," Zann said.

121
00:06:25.374 --> 00:06:26.755
"Let's just get some sleep."

122
00:06:27.595 --> 00:06:29.557
The goon shrugged and took another drink.

123
00:06:29.577 --> 00:06:32.940
"Maybe the boy's right," he said.

124
00:06:32.960 --> 00:06:34.622
"It's getting late."

125
00:06:35.702 --> 00:06:36.743
Krub yawned.

126
00:06:37.864 --> 00:06:41.067
"One of us should stand guard in case those chupos come back.

127
00:06:41.567 --> 00:06:42.929
You can take the first watch."

128
00:06:42.949 --> 00:06:44.930
"Why me?"

129
00:06:45.351 --> 00:06:46.472
the other man complained.

130
00:06:46.492 --> 00:06:47.993
"You do it."

131
00:06:48.834 --> 00:06:51.116
Zann lay down and closed his eyes.

132
00:06:51.945 --> 00:06:54.331
It had been a long day, and he was tired.

133
00:06:54.953 --> 00:06:59.065
As the two men continued to argue, he quickly fell asleep.
